==Finnish==
{{wikipedia|lang=fi|norsut}}

===Etymology===
Originally a synonym (or rather a dialectal variant) of {{m|fi|mursu||walrus}} (see it for more).<ref>Kaisa Häkkinen: "Mursun ja norsun jäljillä", Virittäjä 4/2007 pp. 482–500</ref> Before detailed information about the elephant spread to Finland, it was only known as a big, thick-skinned animal with handsome tusks, hence the initial confusion. The meanings diverged around 18th century.

